Web source  : web/src/features/charging/pages/CostAnalysisPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the cache-then-network data port, also Microsoft.UI-free),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view).
  The generated prompt's idealized "CostAnalysisPage.xaml + CostAnalysisPageViewModel.cs under
  TeslaSync/Features/Charging" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4
  ShellPageFactory by route name ("CostAnalysis"), which RouteTable.cs already maps to /cost-analysis and the
  /charging/costs hidden deep link.
- Data source 1 (web useChargingSessionsPaginated · GET /charging/sessions?vehicle_id=…): ported as the
  Microsoft.UI-free ICostAnalysisSessionsSource. The repository-backed CostAnalysisSessionsSource resolves the
  scoped/primary vehicle via the shared IWidgetVehicleSource (native useSelectedVehicle) and runs one
  cache-then-network read of the generated operation Operations.Charging.Sessions through the shared
  CacheThenNetworkEngine (cacheKey charging:{id}:cost-analysis), parsing each emission into a tolerant
  CostAnalysisSession list via CostAnalysisResultMapper. The session count gates the page's loading/empty/
  success states exactly as the web page's `if (isLoading) … if (!sessions || length === 0) … else …`.
- Data source 2 (web useCostForecast · GET /analytics/cost-forecast [vehicle_id, months]): in the native
  architecture the forecast fetch lives inside the self-fetching CostForecastSection / ForecastDetails child
  surfaces (each with its own repository-backed Source), so the page realises useCostForecast by composing
  those children rather than re-fetching at the page level. No HTTP touches the page view.
- The page is the single aggregation owner the web page is: CostAnalysisAggregator (a Microsoft.UI-free port
  of the chart-feeding slice of web useCostAnalysisData) folds the session list into the four presentational
  chart models — the monthly cost buckets, the per-session cost-per-kWh trend and the charger-type breakdown —
  that the MonthlyCostChart / CostPerKwhChart / ChargerTypeBreakdown / MonthlyCostTable children render. SI
  energy is converted to display kWh only at aggregation time (watt-hours ÷ 1000, the web
  convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh') boundary); cost is the account currency. The default gas price ($3.50/gal) and
  efficiency (30 mpg) from constants.ts seed the monthly gas-equivalent line so the first paint matches the web.
- Section composition (web order/grouping, every <GlassPanel>/region reproduced): the success layout composes
  the existing Fluent child surfaces — CostSummaryCards; [MonthlyCostChart | CostPerKwhChart]; ChargerTypeBreakdown;
  SavingsCalculator; MonthlyCostTable; TimeOfUseAnalysis; CostForecastSection + ForecastDetails (useCostForecast);
  [LifetimeSummary | EnvironmentalImpact]. The seven self-fetching surfaces are built via their Create(deps)
  factories from a CostAnalysisSurfaceDependencies bundle; the four presentational charts are fed the
  page-computed models. The parameterless CostAnalysisPage() defaults to EmptyCostAnalysisSessionsSource (renders
  the empty state) — the established W7 default-feed pattern — while CostAnalysisPage(source, localizer, deps)
  drives the full loading/empty/error/success matrix for DI hosts and the headless tests.
- AICostForecastNarration (web import @/components/ai/AICostForecastNarration) has no W3 component port in-repo
  (the only AI narration surfaces are AITCONarration / AIYearReviewNarration); it is a separate cross-cutting AI
  parity unit and is therefore out of this page's composition scope. This does not narrow the page's declared
  parity (the 7 manifest items + the two data sources are all delivered).
- Catalog: 3 of the 4 page-level i18n keys already existed verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw
  (translation.costAnalysis.{title,subtitle,empty.title}). ONE key was missing and was added, in sorted
  position, to all three locale catalogs (en/ar/he): translation.costAnalysis.empty.message (English text
  seeded; resolves verbatim via ILocalizer / the web key name).
- Pre-existing build-blocker fixed (required to verify this page): the W4 shell registration constructor
  ShellWindow.xaml.cs carried two malformed lambdas in the committed baseline — the "YearReview" and
  "AutomationList" PageFactory.Register lambdas were missing their `return page; });` closure (confirmed
  pre-existing via `git diff`: this prompt's only registration line is +2). The whole App C# assembly therefore
  failed to compile (CS1026 at the constructor's closing brace), which in turn crashed the XAML markup compiler
  (WMC9999) with a cascade of "unknown type" errors. The two obviously-intended closures were completed
  (matching the adjacent, well-formed "Automations" lambda) — a behaviour-neutral fix returning the
  already-constructed page — so the file/assembly compiles and the gate can run.

